GitHub Pages checks only for this file's presence, not its content, so it's
safe to leave this note here for future reference.

Added 2026-10-22: this repo is plain static output from ActualNews's
WebsiteBackend.py, not a Jekyll site (no _config.yml, front matter, or
Liquid). Without .nojekyll, GitHub still ran every push through its
legacy Jekyll build step for no reason -- added cost, and the proximate
cause of an observed "Page build failed" on one push (duration 0ms)
that an unrelated identical push built fine 14 minutes later. This file
tells Pages to serve the files as-is instead.
